abstract: "GUS defines a regular calendar kernel (364-day common year, 371-day Gran Tempalum year) plus a continuous instant scale and an optional notary anchoring layer with post-quantum signatures (SLH-DSA / FIPS 205). Three independent implementations (Python, JavaScript, C) conform to a single normative vector set."
keywords:
  - calendar
  - timestamp
  - post-quantum
  - cryptography
  - time
repository-code: "https://github.com/verared/gerarion"

